{"title":"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square with side length 8 cm. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8712c1ef923b8ffd7923e7e481ed3091b5944113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is right-angled at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8712c1ef923b8ffd7923e7e481ed3091b5944113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is 30% of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, what is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since opposite sides of a rectangle are equal in length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b75667e975d187b85b9eccd20878f939ead2e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = BC = 8 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, the area is equal its side length times itself, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/3436d4def235565b72e150cbadd87839d2f313af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 8 = 64 \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8712c1ef923b8ffd7923e7e481ed3091b5944113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of this, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8712c1ef923b8ffd7923e7e481ed3091b5944113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc08f0d90f765138891473ffd7a946a751b8b9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\% \\times 64 = \\frac{3}{10} \\times 64 = \\frac{192}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>For any triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4ae681c4cf5ec73b7d8dc2a5fa638e9da45ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area of the triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the base of the triangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the height of the triangle. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb10ab75cba44618506c07af66ff0aa16bd2cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{192}{10} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times AE \\times 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de045269ab516375cd5257a37cbc5b86966e62f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4AE = \\frac{192}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056eaa218ad0f7d1aa13f8cc0c58af99b4666e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = \\frac{\\frac{192}{4}}{10} = \\frac{48}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7da882f12cf4f986dbcdc418d1381b526096fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{4.8 \\text{ cm}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC\" title=\"2017 CSMC\">2017 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061558\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\